# Config XML root names

When creating a 7D2D **Config** xpath patch `.xml` (including `XUi_InGame` / `XUi_Menu`), the wrapper root is:

`AGF` + `-` + the **last hyphen segment** of `ModInfo.xml` `<Name>` (no version, no folder suffix).

Drop `zzz` and every middle token (`Requested`, `VP`, `VPS`, `NoEAC`, `HUDPlus`, `4Modders`, `Special`, …). Always start with `AGF`, never `zzzAGF`.

| ModInfo Name | Root |
|---|---|
| `AGF-Requested-AnimalTrackerAlwaysOn` | `<AGF-AnimalTrackerAlwaysOn>` |
| `zzzAGF-Requested-LootStaysOnEmpty` | `<AGF-LootStaysOnEmpty>` |
| `AGF-NoEAC-MapPlus` | `<AGF-MapPlus>` |
| `AGF-HUDPlus-VisualEntityTracker` | `<AGF-VisualEntityTracker>` |
| `AGF-VP-DoorsPlus` | `<AGF-DoorsPlus>` |
| `zzzAGF-Special-Compatibilities` | `<AGF-Compatibilities>` |

Do not use `<configs>`, `<config>`, the folder name, or the versioned folder.

## Existing mods

If the mod already has Config XML, **reuse that root** on new files in the same mod. Do not rename old roots unless asked.

## Not this rule

- `ModInfo.xml` stays `<xml>`
- Non-xpath files owned by a DLL (custom settings XML) keep their own root
